<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11384" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cosmĭcŏs</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοσμικός</span>
		(syn. mundanus), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the world;</i> as <i>subst.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cosmĭcŏs</span></b> ,
				i, m., <i>a citizen of
				the world, a cosmopolite</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 7,
				41, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cosmĭca</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., <i>worldly things</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 7, 41, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
